{
  "schema": "clearance-feature-recovery-1",
  "status": "implemented-qa-in-progress",
  "commit": "423462a",
  "scope": "Robustness to a 116-pixel (0.0725%) resampling perturbation in a fixed 400x400 learned development mask; cropping and slit-count candidates held unchanged. Not an original-artwork accuracy claim.",
  "findings": [
    "The perturbed 4x4 alternative has a lower clearance score but misses a source colour region; the old feature-retention gate prevents its bounded repair.",
    "Simply enabling refinement is insufficient: its initially valid paper creates a safe rollback point. Useful later checkpoints are uncertain at 360px, and repeated rollbacks discard their progress.",
    "A fixed 125-step comparison on identical curves reduces independent error from 6.9475% to 1.849375% when the existing finer paper verification is enabled.",
    "A final uncertain checkpoint can miss the in-loop time reserve. The helper now evaluates this retained candidate against the original source and independently audits its actual curves at 700px before accepting it."
  ],
  "changes": [
    "Allow one lower-scoring, geometry-valid alternative with missing source colours into the bounded helper when no image-passing candidate exists. Immediate promotion still requires retained features.",
    "Use the main fitter's paper verification before rollback; preserve the same 1.2-second overall helper cap and ten-second search deadline.",
    "Compare the retained uncertain checkpoint and incumbent using original-source error; retain complete geometry, feature and material checks. Crossings, weighted borders and requested symmetry remain excluded."
  ],
